in [1 - 100] [90]  \r\n                              JPEG quality in 1..100. Default 90; invalid for PNG.\r\n          --max-frames INT:INT in [1 - 5000] \r\n                              Maximum output frame count in 1..5000. Optional.\r\n          --backend TEXT:{auto,ffmpeg,ve_frame_reader,ve-frame-reader} \r\n                              Frame extraction backend. Omit for runner default; use ffmpeg\r\n                              only when the caller explicitly needs it.\r\n          --no-auto-orient    Disable display matrix / rotation metadata normalization.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media extract-frames --input /tmp/in.mp4 --output-dir /tmp/frames --start 0s --end 10s --interval 500ms --width 640 --height 360\r\n  $ lyra-cli media extract-frames --input /tmp/in.mp4 --output-dir /tmp/frames --timestamp 1s --timestamp 2.5s --format png\r\n  $ lyra-cli media extract-frames --input /tmp/in.mp4 --output-dir /tmp/frames --interval 1s --short-side 360\r\n\r\nTIME LITERALS\r\n  Explicit units are required; values accept `2min`, `1.5s`, `500ms`, or `1200000us`.\r\n  Bare numbers and `m` are invalid.\r\n  Repeatable --timestamp mode is exclusive of range/interval/max-frames.\r\n  --end and --duration are mutually exclusive.\r\n  --short-side cannot coexist with --width/--height.\r\n  Input display-matrix rotation is applied to output pixels automatically.\r\n  --max-frames stops decoding immediately after the requested frame count.\r\n",
